@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About Us";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Why ZapWatch exists, and who's building it.";
}

<p class="zw-eyebrow mb-1">About</p>
<h1 class="mb-4">Built by one freelancer, for people doing the same work.</h1>

<div class="zw-card p-4 p-md-5" style="max-width:760px;">
    <p>
        I'm Anseer. ZapWatch started from the same question that's been asked, on and off, on
        Zapier's own community forum since 2021: how do you catch a client's Zap that just&hellip;
        stopped, without building a heartbeat table and a watchdog Zap by hand for every single
        client automation you maintain. Nobody had shipped a real answer &mdash; just the same
        DIY pattern, rebuilt from scratch by whoever hit the problem next. That's the whole reason
        this exists.
    </p>

    <h3>Who's building it</h3>
    <p>
        Right now, just me, in weekday evening blocks and a few hours on Saturdays &mdash; not a
        funded team. That's not a caveat I'm hiding; it's context worth knowing if you're deciding
        whether to trust a client's alerting to this. It also means I've been deliberate about
        where the corners get cut and where they don't: the watchdog logic that decides whether an
        automation has actually gone quiet, and the payment path that activates your subscription,
        both get real automated tests, not just a manual click-through. Everything else &mdash;
        screens, copy, polish &mdash; ships at a rougher, faster pace on purpose. If something's
        going to quietly break your trust in this product, it's not going to be a typo on the
        pricing page.
    </p>

    <h3>What this isn't</h3>
    <p>
        This isn't trying to be a general-purpose uptime or cron monitor with a Zapier skin bolted
        on. It's built narrowly for Zapier freelancers and small agencies watching client
        automations, in Zapier's own vocabulary, and it stays that way on purpose &mdash; Make and
        n8n support, Shopify/QuickBooks-specific polling, and a few other things are deliberately
        out of scope for now rather than half-built everywhere.
    </p>

    <h3>Get in touch</h3>
    <p class="mb-0">
        Questions, bug reports, or just want to tell me what's missing:
        <a href="mailto:iamanseernk@gmail.com">iamanseernk@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
</div>
